**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A study's experiments fall into session blocks, split automatically at the Diagnostic runs or set by hand, and a session's dark comes from the Dark runs (001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data: auto-split at Diagnostic experiments, or by hand; … dark from the Dark runs'; the S11.1 brief 'Sessions, auto-split at DiagnosticRun experiments or set by hand'; step 285: a hand-set `SessionName` is the session a run belongs to, the rest split at the Diagnostic runs). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after `SessionGainModel.ruleWith` (step 356): (1) `StudySession = { name : SessionName; experiments : ExperimentName list }`, one session block. (2) `static member splitAll (experiments : Experiment list) : StudySession list`, over the experiments in the order given: an experiment whose `sessionOpt` is `Some s` (`SetExperimentSession`, step 294) joins the session named `s`; a `DiagnosticRun` (step 285) with no hand-set session belongs to no session and closes the current automatic block; every other experiment joins the current automatic block. Each non-empty automatic block is a session named `Session <k>`, `k` the smallest positive integer whose `SessionName` neither a hand-set session of the list nor an earlier block holds, so two Diagnostic runs in a row, or one at either end, make no empty session. The sessions are ordered by the position of their first experiment, each holding its experiments in list order. (3) `member this.darkRunsIn (experiments : Experiment list) : ExperimentName list`: the session's `DarkRun` experiments in its order, or, when it holds none, every `DarkRun` experiment of `experiments` in their order, because one darkness file can serve every session (the optics-mueller kit's `darkness_checks.csv`, step 330). Reading the dark level from those runs' data is the forward model's (S11.2). No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `StudySessionTests` (step 356), over test-local experiments built as `ExperimentProxyTests`' fixtures build them, differing only in name, role and session: `experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own`: E1 (Science), E2 (Calibration), D1 (Diagnostic), E3 (Science), E4 (Science, hand-set `Day 2`), E5 (Dark) and D2 (Diagnostic) split into `Session 1` [E1; E2], `Session 2` [E3; E5] and `Day 2` [E4], in that order; the same list with E1 hand-set to `Session 1` gives `Session 1` [E1], `Session 2` [E2] and `Session 3` [E3; E5] and `Day 2` [E4], ordered by first experiment; and a list of only Diagnostic runs gives no session. `a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study`: in the first split, `Session 2`'s dark runs are [E5], and `Session 1`'s and `Day 2`'s are every Dark run of the list, [E5]; a session holding two Dark runs answers its own two.

**Acceptance.** After sessions land, `StudySession.splitAll` MUST gather hand-set sessions, split the rest at each Diagnostic run into `Session <k>` blocks ordered by their first experiment, and `darkRunsIn` MUST answer a session's own Dark runs or else every Dark run; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own` and `a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
